{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Cell \u2014 chunks+handtuned+seeded @ \u03b1=1.0 + ChunkAbortGate (v5.3 Phase D ablation)",
    "description": "Phase v5.3 Phase E \u2014 chunk seeding.  Inherits Phase C's handtuned scaffold and pre-loads MotorRepertoire with 4 hand-authored intent-sequence chunks so the substrate has a non-random library of behaviours to dispatch from tick 1.\n\nSeeded chunks (intent index \u2192 Premotor's bilateral table at L=[+4,+2,+4,0,-4], R=[-4,0,+4,+2,+4]):\n  - chunk seed 1 'scent_seek_forward' = [2]*20 (forward straight, default)\n  - chunk seed 2 'arc_left_scan'      = [1]*12 + [2]*8 (soft-left arc then forward)\n  - chunk seed 3 'arc_right_scan'     = [3]*12 + [2]*8 (mirror)\n  - chunk seed 4 'hard_pivot'         = [0,0,0,4,4,4]*3 + [0,0] (alternating hard-left/hard-right spin)\n\nAll seeds get trigger_motif=-1 (wildcard \u2014 fire under any consensus context) and replay_hits=2 (Beta(1,1) score = (2+1)/(2+0+0+2) = 0.75 \u2192 above 0.5 commit threshold, immediately dispatchable).  Negative chunk_ids distinguish seeds from organic crystallisations.\n\nA/B (vs handtuned-only) tests whether having a non-random chunk library at startup measurably changes behaviour.  Decision gate: \u0394 >= +1 hit at p < 0.30 \u2192 seeding is the missing piece.  Null \u2192 substrate doesn't make use of seeds either; bottleneck is upstream (chunks themselves not the right unit, or organic crystallisation already saturates the chunk pool fast enough).",
    "env_target": "cell",
    "phase_tag": "v5.3-seeded-a100-abort",
    "reflex_modular": true,
    "body_model": "differential_paddler",
    "episode_length": 3600
  },
  "version": 1,
  "runtime": {
    "thread_pool": "per_instance",
    "num_threads": 0
  },
